%T A123415 93855915733
%N A123415 Number of cograph contraction perfect graphs on n nodes.
%C A123415 A graph G is a cograph contraction if there is a cograph H and pairwise disjoint stable sets of H such that G is obtained from H by contracting each of the stable sets to a single vertex and joining the new vertices pairwise. Cograph contractions are perfect, every cograph is a cograph contraction, and the class is closed under induced subgraphs. - _Meghanto Majumder_, Oct 08 2026
%H A123415 S. Hougardy, <a href="http://www.or.uni-bonn.de/~hougardy/">Home Page</a>
%H A123415 S. Hougardy, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.disc.2006.05.021">Classes of perfect graphs</a>, Discr. Math. 306 (2006), 2529-2571.
%H A123415 Van Bang Le, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1002/(SICI)1097-0118(199904)30:4%3C309::AID-JGT5%3E3.0.CO;2-5">A good characterization of cograph contractions</a>, J. Graph Theory 30 (1999), 309-318.
%Y A123415 Cf. A000088, A052431 (perfect graphs), A000084 (cographs).
